'\" t
.nh
.TH podman-network-prune 1
.SH "نام (NAME)"
podman-network-prune \- Remove all unused networks

.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBpodman network prune\fP [\fIoptions\fP]

.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Remove all unused networks.  An unused network is defined by a network which
has no containers connected or configured to connect to it. It does not remove
the so-called default network which goes by the name of \fIpodman\fP\&.

.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.SS \fB--filter\fP
Provide filter values.

.PP
If there is more than one filter, the \fB--filter\fR option should be passed multiple times: \fB--filter\fP \fIlabel=test\fP \fB--filter\fP \fIuntil=10m\fP\&.

.PP
Supported filters:

.TS
allbox;
l l 
l l .
\fBFilter\fP	\fBDescription\fP
label	T{
Only remove networks, with (or without, in the case of label!=[...] is used) the specified labels.
T}
until	T{
Only remove networks created before given timestamp.
T}
.TE

.PP
The \fBlabel\fR \fIfilter\fP accepts two formats. One is the \fBlabel\fR=\fIkey\fP or \fBlabel\fR=\fIkey\fP=\fIvalue\fP, which removes networks with the specified labels. The other format is the \fBlabel!\fR=\fIkey\fP or \fBlabel!\fR=\fIkey\fP=\fIvalue\fP, which removes networks without the specified labels.

.PP
The \fBuntil\fR \fIfilter\fP can be Unix timestamps, date formatted timestamps, or Go duration strings (e.g. 10m, 1h30m) computed relative to the machine’s time.

.SS \fB--force\fP, \fB-f\fP
Do not prompt for confirmation

.SH "مثال (EXAMPLE)"
Prune networks:

.EX
podman network prune
.EE

.PP
Prune all networks created not created in the last two hours:

.EX
podman network prune --filter until=2h
.EE

.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBpodman(1)\fP, \fBpodman-network(1)\fP, \fBpodman-network-rm(1)\fP

